HIGH-01: CORS Misconfiguration on Ably REST API (main.realtime.ably.net)
========================================
Severity: HIGH
CVSS 4.0: 7.5 (AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N)
CVSS 3.1: 7.5 (AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:N)

Description:
The Ably REST API at https://main.realtime.ably.net reflects arbitrary Origin headers in Access-Control-Allow-Origin response header while setting Access-Control-Allow-Credentials: true. This affects all authenticated endpoints including:
- /time
- /stats
- /channels/{channelId}/messages
- /channels (enumeration)
- /keys
- /push/deviceRegistrations
- All other authenticated endpoints

When a user is authenticated (via Basic auth or token), any malicious website can make authenticated cross-origin requests and read responses, leading to:
- Full account takeover via API key theft
- Message history exfiltration
- Channel enumeration
- Push notification device registration abuse
- Real-time data interception

Affected Base URL: https://main.realtime.ably.net

Evidence:
$ curl -I -H "Origin: https://evil.com" https://main.realtime.ably.net/time
HTTP/2 200
access-control-allow-origin: https://evil.com
access-control-allow-credentials: true
access-control-expose-headers: Link,Transfer-Encoding,Content-Length,X-Ably-ErrorCode,X-Ably-ErrorMessage,X-Ably-ServerId,X-Ably-Cluster,Server,X-Amz-Cf-Pop
vary: Origin
x-ably-cluster: prod:realtime:main
via: 1.1 cloudfront (CloudFront)

The Vary: Origin header confirms dynamic Origin reflection. With credentials allowed, any website can make authenticated requests.

Impact:
- API key theft (Basic auth credentials in Authorization header)
- Token theft (Bearer tokens)
- Full message history access across all channels
- Channel enumeration and metadata access
- Push device registration manipulation
- Real-time presence data access
- Account takeover via key rotation

Reproduction Steps:
1. Victim has valid Ably API key (Basic auth) or token
2. Victim visits attacker-controlled page
3. Page makes fetch() with credentials: 'include' to main.realtime.ably.net/time
4. Response readable by attacker JavaScript
5. Attacker can then enumerate channels, read messages, steal keys

Proof of Concept:
See attached ably_poc_high01.html

Remediation:
- Implement strict allowlist of allowed origins (ably.com, app.ably.com, dashboard.ably.com)
- Never reflect arbitrary Origin header
- Remove Access-Control-Allow-Credentials: true from authenticated endpoints
- Implement CSRF tokens for state-changing operations
- Consider separate CORS policies for public vs authenticated endpoints

